IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-nouns`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1984 (Western Australia) -- PART II: GENERAL INTERPRETATION PROVISIONS, ss 6 to 19
-- (section 5, the definitions, is in wa-interpretation-s5-definitions.l4).
-- Each rule of reading is a function over a small typed description of what the rule operates on.  Where the
-- Act hands a judgment to the reader (whether a relationship is "marriagelike", whether a construction "promotes
-- the purpose or object"), the judgment is a plain input.  Where the text does not reach a case the result is
-- NOTHING (the explicit "not covered" value), never FALSE.

§ `Part II -- General interpretation provisions`

§§ `6. Definitions in a written law, application of`

DECLARE `Where a provision stands in relation to a definition or rule of interpretation` IS ONE OF
    `it is a provision that contains the definition or rule`
    `it is another provision of the same written law`
    `it is a provision of a different written law`

-- Section 6: definitions or rules of interpretation in a written law apply to the provisions that contain them as
-- well as to other provisions of that written law.  Another written law is not reached (NOTHING).
-- src:259 | Definitions or rules of interpretation contained in a written law apply to the construction of the provisions of the written law that contain those definitions or rules of interpretation as well as to other provisions of that written law.
@ref s 6 (src:259)
GIVEN w IS A `Where a provision stands in relation to a definition or rule of interpretation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a definition or rule of interpretation applies to the provision` w MEANS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `it is a provision that contains the definition or rule` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `it is another provision of the same written law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `it is a provision of a different written law` THEN NOTHING

§§ `7. Written laws to be construed subject to State's legislative power`

DECLARE `Extent of validity of an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `valid in full`
    `valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of the State`

-- Section 7: every written law is construed subject to the limits of the legislative power of the State and so as
-- not to exceed it, to the intent that where an enactment would otherwise be construed as in excess of that power
-- it is nevertheless valid to the extent to which it is not in excess.
-- src:261 | Every written law shall be construed subject to the limits of the legislative power of the State and so as not to exceed that power to the intent that where any enactment thereof, but for this section, would be construed as being in excess of that power, it shall nevertheless be valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of that power.
@ref s 7 (src:261)
GIVEN `any of the enactment would, but for this section, be construed as in excess of the legislative power of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Extent of validity of an enactment`
`the extent of validity of an enactment` `any of the enactment would, but for this section, be construed as in excess of the legislative power of the State` MEANS
    IF `any of the enactment would, but for this section, be construed as in excess of the legislative power of the State`
    THEN `valid to the extent to which it is not in excess of the legislative power of the State`
    ELSE `valid in full`

§§ `8. Written laws always speaking`

-- Section 8: a written law is considered as always speaking, and whenever a matter or thing is expressed in the
-- present tense it is applied to the circumstances as they arise.  For a circumstance that arose before the written
-- law came into operation the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:263 | A written law shall be considered as always speaking and whenever a matter or thing is expressed in the present tense, it shall be applied to the circumstances as they arise, so that effect may be given to every part of the law according to its true spirit, intent, and meaning.
@ref s 8 (src:263)
GIVEN `the day the circumstance arises` IS A DATE
      `the day the written law came into operation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a present tense provision applies to the circumstance as it arises` `the day the circumstance arises` `the day the written law came into operation` MEANS
    IF Day `the day the circumstance arises` AT LEAST Day `the day the written law came into operation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `9. Parts of speech and grammatical forms`

-- Section 9: where a word or phrase is defined in a written law, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of
-- it have corresponding meanings.  A word that is not another form of the defined word is not reached (NOTHING).
-- src:265 | Where a word or phrase is defined in a written law, other parts of speech and grammatical forms of that word or phrase have corresponding meanings.
@ref s 9 (src:265)
GIVEN `the word is another part of speech or grammatical form of the defined word or phrase` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the word has a corresponding meaning` `the word is another part of speech or grammatical form of the defined word or phrase` MEANS
    IF `the word is another part of speech or grammatical form of the defined word or phrase` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `10. Gender and number`

DECLARE `What a gendered word is asked about` IS ONE OF
    `an individual, of any gender or sex`
    `a person that is not an individual`
    `something that is not a person`

DECLARE `Number of a word` IS ONE OF
    `singular`
    `plural`

-- Section 10(a): words that indicate or could be taken to indicate a person of a particular gender or sex (for
-- example, he, she, chairman, workman) include any individual, regardless of gender or sex, and any person that is
-- not an individual.  Paragraph (b) is shown as deleted.
-- src:268 | (a) words that indicate or could be taken to indicate a person of a particular gender or sex (for example, he, she, chairman, workman) include —
-- src:269 | (i) any individual, regardless of gender or sex; and
-- src:270 | (ii) any person that is not an individual;
@ref s 10(a) (src:268-270)
GIVEN x IS A `What a gendered word is asked about`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a word indicating a person of a particular gender or sex includes` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `an individual, of any gender or sex` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a person that is not an individual` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something that is not a person` THEN NOTHING

-- Section 10(c): words in the singular number include the plural and words in the plural number include the
-- singular.
-- src:272 | (c) words in the singular number include the plural and words in the plural number include the singular.
@ref s 10(c) (src:272)
GIVEN n IS A `Number of a word`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Number of a word`
`the numbers a word in this number covers` n MEANS
    LIST `singular`, `plural`

§§ `11. Sovereign, references to`

-- Section 11: a reference in a written law to the Sovereign reigning at the time the law was enacted or made, or to
-- the Crown, is construed as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being.
-- src:275 | A reference in a written law to the Sovereign reigning at the time the law was enacted or made, or to the Crown, shall be construed as a reference to the Sovereign for the time being.
@ref s 11 (src:275)
GIVEN `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning when the law was enacted or made, or to the Crown` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Sovereign for the time being` IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the Sovereign meant by the reference` `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning when the law was enacted or made, or to the Crown` `the Sovereign for the time being` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to the Sovereign reigning when the law was enacted or made, or to the Crown`
    THEN JUST `the Sovereign for the time being`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `12. Minister, references to`

-- Section 12: a reference in a written law to the Minister is construed (a) in an Act, as the Minister of the Crown
-- to whom the Governor has for the time being committed the administration of the Act or of the provision; (b) in
-- subsidiary legislation, as the Minister to whom the administration of the Act or provision under which it is made
-- is for the time being committed; and (c) so as to include a Minister of the Crown for the time being acting for or on
-- behalf of that Minister.  Who the Minister is, is a borrowed fact.
-- src:277 | A reference in a written law to the Minister shall be construed —
-- src:278 | (a) in the case of a reference in an Act, as a reference to the Minister of the Crown to whom the administration of the Act, or the provision of the Act, in which or in respect of which the term is used, is for the time being committed by the Governor; and
-- src:279 | (b) in the case of a reference in subsidiary legislation, as a reference to the Minister of the Crown to whom the administration of the Act, or the provision of the Act, under which the subsidiary legislation is made, is for the time being committed by the Governor; and
-- src:280 | (c) so as to include a Minister of the Crown for the time being acting for or on behalf of the Minister referred to in paragraph (a) or (b), as the case may require.
@ref s 12 (src:277-280)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of written law`
      `the Minister to whom the Governor has for the time being committed the administration of the Act or provision` IS A STRING
      `a Minister for the time being acting for or on behalf of that Minister, if any` IS A MAYBE STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the Ministers a reference to the Minister covers` kind `the Minister to whom the Governor has for the time being committed the administration of the Act or provision` `a Minister for the time being acting for or on behalf of that Minister, if any` MEANS
    CONSIDER `a Minister for the time being acting for or on behalf of that Minister, if any`
    WHEN JUST acting THEN LIST `the Minister to whom the Governor has for the time being committed the administration of the Act or provision`, acting
    WHEN NOTHING THEN LIST `the Minister to whom the Governor has for the time being committed the administration of the Act or provision`

§§ `13. British subject etc., references to`

-- Section 13(1): in section 13, "Commonwealth Act" means the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 of the Parliament of the
-- Commonwealth, as amended, and "law of the State" means a written law in force in the State.  (Section 5 defines
-- "Commonwealth Act" differently for the rest of the written laws; this meaning is limited to section 13.)
-- src:283 | Commonwealth Act means the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 3 of the Parliament of the Commonwealth, as amended;
-- src:284 | law of the State means a written law in force in the State.
@ref s 13(1) (src:283-284)
GIVETH A STRING
`the Act that Commonwealth Act means in section 13` MEANS "Australian Citizenship Act 1948"

@ref s 13(1) (src:284)
GIVEN `it is a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in force in the State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a law of the State` `it is a written law` `it is in force in the State` MEANS
    `it is a written law` AND `it is in force in the State`

DECLARE `Status of a person under the Commonwealth citizenship Act` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian citizen`
    `a person who has the status of a British subject under the Commonwealth Act`
    `a person who has the status of a British subject without citizenship under the Commonwealth Act`
    `a person with none of those statuses`

-- Section 13(2): a reference in any law of the State to a British subject, or a natural born or naturalized subject
-- of Her Majesty, or any like expression, is read as a reference to an Australian citizen and to any other person
-- who, under the Commonwealth Act, has the status of a British subject or of a British subject without citizenship.
-- Section 13(3): a rule of law that applies to a British subject applies to such a person as if a British subject.
-- The Commonwealth Act is the Australian Citizenship Act 1948 "as amended"; footnote 3 of the text says that Act is
-- repealed and replaced by the Australian Citizenship Act 2007.  The status is a borrowed fact.
-- src:285 | (2) A reference in any law of the State to a British subject or to a natural born or naturalized subject of Her Majesty or to any other like expression, shall be read as a reference to an Australian citizen and to any other person who, under the Commonwealth Act, has the status of a British subject or has the status of a British subject without citizenship.
-- src:286 | (3) Where a rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to a British subject, that rule of law applies to, or in relation to, or has effect with respect to an Australian citizen and any other person who, under the Commonwealth Act, has the status of a British subject or has the status of a British subject without citizenship, as if that Australian citizen or other person were a British subject.
@ref s 13(2) (src:285)
@ref s 13(3) (src:286)
GIVEN x IS A `Status of a person under the Commonwealth citizenship Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to a British subject is read as a reference to the person` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `an Australian citizen` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person who has the status of a British subject under the Commonwealth Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person who has the status of a British subject without citizenship under the Commonwealth Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person with none of those statuses` THEN FALSE

@ref s 13(3) (src:286)
GIVEN x IS A `Status of a person under the Commonwealth citizenship Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a rule of law about British subjects applies to the person as if a British subject` x MEANS
    `a reference to a British subject is read as a reference to the person` x

§§ `13A. De facto relationship and de facto partner, references to`

DECLARE `Indicators of a de facto relationship` HAS
    `the length of the relationship between them points to one`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the two persons have resided together`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the nature and extent of their common residence points to one`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is, or has been, a sexual relationship between them`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and arrangements for support, point to one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the ownership, use and acquisition of their property points to one`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the degree of mutual commitment by them to a shared life points to one`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `they care for and support children`                                                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the reputation and public aspects of the relationship point to one`                     IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 13A(1): a reference in a written law to a de facto relationship is a reference to a relationship (other
-- than a legal marriage) between 2 persons who live together in a marriagelike relationship.  Section 13A(3): it
-- does not matter whether the persons are different sexes or the same sex, or whether either is legally married to
-- someone else or in another de facto relationship.  Whether they live together in a marriagelike relationship
-- is the judgment the Act hands to the reader: a plain input.
-- src:288 | (1) A reference in a written law to a de facto relationship shall be construed as a reference to a relationship (other than a legal marriage) between 2 persons who live together in a marriagelike relationship.
-- src:299 | (3) It does not matter whether —
-- src:300 | (a) the persons are different sexes or the same sex; or
-- src:301 | (b) either of the persons is legally married to someone else or in another de facto relationship.
@ref s 13A(1) (src:288)
@ref s 13A(3) (src:299-301)
GIVEN `the two persons live together in a marriagelike relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relationship is a legal marriage between them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are of different sexes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `either is legally married to someone else or in another de facto relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a de facto relationship exists between two persons` `the two persons live together in a marriagelike relationship` `the relationship is a legal marriage between them` `they are of different sexes` `either is legally married to someone else or in another de facto relationship` MEANS
        `the two persons live together in a marriagelike relationship`
    AND (NOT `the relationship is a legal marriage between them`)

-- Section 13A(2): the nine factors are indicators of whether or not a de facto relationship exists, but are not
-- essential.  They are counted for the reader and do not enter `a de facto relationship exists between two persons`.
-- src:289 | (2) The following factors are indicators of whether or not a de facto relationship exists between 2 persons, but are not essential —
-- src:290 | (a) the length of the relationship between them;
-- src:291 | (b) whether the 2 persons have resided together;
-- src:292 | (c) the nature and extent of common residence;
-- src:293 | (d) whether there is, or has been, a sexual relationship between them;
-- src:294 | (e) the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangements for financial support, between them;
-- src:295 | (f) the ownership, use and acquisition of their property (including property they own individually);
-- src:296 | (g) the degree of mutual commitment by them to a shared life;
-- src:297 | (h) whether they care for and support children;
-- src:298 | (i) the reputation, and public aspects, of the relationship between them.
@ref s 13A(2) (src:289-298)
GIVEN x IS A `Indicators of a de facto relationship`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of indicators present` x MEANS
      (IF x's `the length of the relationship between them points to one` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF x's `the two persons have resided together` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF x's `the nature and extent of their common residence points to one` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF x's `there is, or has been, a sexual relationship between them` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF x's `the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and arrangements for support, point to one` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF x's `the ownership, use and acquisition of their property points to one` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF x's `the degree of mutual commitment by them to a shared life points to one` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF x's `they care for and support children` THEN 1 ELSE 0)
    + (IF x's `the reputation and public aspects of the relationship point to one` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- Section 13A(4): a reference to a de facto partner is a reference to a person who lives, or where the context
-- requires has lived, in a de facto relationship.
-- src:302 | (4) A reference in a written law to a de facto partner shall be construed as a reference to a person who lives, or where the context requires, has lived, in a de facto relationship.
@ref s 13A(4) (src:302)
GIVEN lives IS A BOOLEAN
      `has lived` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the context requires has lived` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is a de facto partner` lives `has lived` `the context requires has lived` MEANS
    lives OR (`the context requires has lived` AND `has lived`)

-- Section 13A(5): the de facto partner of the first person is the person who lives, or lived, in the de facto
-- relationship with the first person.
-- src:303 | (5) The de facto partner of a person (the first person) is the person who lives, or lived, in the de facto relationship with the first person.
@ref s 13A(5) (src:303)
GIVEN `the other person lives or lived in a de facto relationship with the first person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the other person is the de facto partner of the first person` `the other person lives or lived in a de facto relationship with the first person` MEANS
    `the other person lives or lived in a de facto relationship with the first person`

§§ `13B. Standards Association of Australia, references to`

-- Section 13B: a reference in a written law (other than this Act) to the Standards Association of Australia is
-- read as a reference to Standards Australia.  In this Act itself the section says nothing (NOTHING).
-- src:306 | A reference in a written law (other than this Act) to the Standards Association of Australia shall be read as a reference to Standards Australia.
@ref s 13B (src:306)
GIVEN `the written law is this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the body a reference to the Standards Association of Australia is read as` `the written law is this Act` MEANS
    IF `the written law is this Act` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST "Standards Australia"

§§ `13CA. Local government districts, references to`

-- Section 13CA(1): in a written law, "local government district" means a district under the Local Government Act 1995.
-- src:309 | (1) In a written law —
-- src:310 | local government district means a district under the Local Government Act 1995.
@ref s 13CA(1) (src:309-310)
GIVEN `it is a district under the Local Government Act 1995` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a local government district` `it is a district under the Local Government Act 1995` MEANS
    `it is a district under the Local Government Act 1995`

-- Section 13CA(2): a reference in a written law to a named local government district is a reference to the
-- district that has that name under the Local Government Act 1995.  The districts that exist under that Act are a
-- borrowed fact (the caller lists their names).  The text's examples: "Perth local government district" refers to
-- the district named Perth; "Narrogin (Shire) local government district" to the district named Narrogin (Shire).
-- src:311 | (2) A reference in a written law to a named local government district is a reference to the local government district that has that name under the Local Government Act 1995.
-- src:313 | 1. “Perth local government district” refers to the local government district named Perth.
-- src:314 | 2. “Narrogin (Shire) local government district” refers to the local government district named Narrogin (Shire).]
@ref s 13CA(2) (src:311-314)
GIVEN name IS A STRING
      `the names of the districts under the Local Government Act 1995` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`the local government district a name refers to` name `the names of the districts under the Local Government Act 1995` MEANS
    IF elem name `the names of the districts under the Local Government Act 1995` THEN JUST name ELSE NOTHING

§§ `13C. When death of a person occurs`

-- Section 13C: for the purposes of the law of this State a person dies when there occurs (a) irreversible cessation
-- of all function of the person's brain; or (b) irreversible cessation of circulation of blood in the person's body.
-- src:317 | For the purposes of the law of this State, a person dies when there occurs —
-- src:318 | (a) irreversible cessation of all function of the person’s brain; or
-- src:319 | (b) irreversible cessation of circulation of blood in the person’s body.
@ref s 13C (src:317-319)
GIVEN `there is irreversible cessation of all function of the person's brain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is irreversible cessation of circulation of blood in the person's body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person has died` `there is irreversible cessation of all function of the person's brain` `there is irreversible cessation of circulation of blood in the person's body` MEANS
        `there is irreversible cessation of all function of the person's brain`
    OR  `there is irreversible cessation of circulation of blood in the person's body`

§§ `13D. Bankrupt and related expressions, references to`

DECLARE `Insolvency facts about a person` HAS
    `bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `a substantially similar status under a law applicable where that Act does not apply`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `a debtor party to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a debtor who has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations remain to be discharged` IS A BOOLEAN
    `not yet in a Part X agreement but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X`   IS A BOOLEAN

-- Section 13D(1): a reference to a person being a bankrupt means the person is a bankrupt as defined in the
-- Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth) or has a substantially similar status under a law applicable in a place
-- where that Act does not apply.
-- src:322 | (1) A reference in a written law to a person being a bankrupt means that the person is a bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth) or has a substantially similar status under a law applicable in a place where that Act does not apply.
@ref s 13D(1) (src:322)
GIVEN x IS A `Insolvency facts about a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a bankrupt` x MEANS
        x's `bankrupt as defined in the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)`
    OR  x's `a substantially similar status under a law applicable where that Act does not apply`

-- Section 13D(2): a reference to a person being a bankrupt or a person whose affairs are under insolvency laws
-- means that (a) the person is a bankrupt as described in (1); or (b) the person is a debtor party to a debt
-- agreement; or (c) the person has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations created
-- by it remain to be discharged; or (d) the person has not yet entered a Part X agreement but has authorised a
-- controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X; or that the person has a substantially similar status
-- under a law applicable where the Bankruptcy Act does not apply.
-- src:323 | (2) A reference in a written law to a person being a bankrupt or a person whose affairs are under insolvency laws means that —
-- src:324 | (a) the person is a bankrupt as described in subsection (1); or
-- src:325 | (b) the person is a party, as a debtor, to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth); or
-- src:326 | (c) the person has, as a debtor, entered into a personal insolvency agreement under Part X of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth) and obligations created by the agreement remain to be discharged; or
-- src:327 | (d) the person has not yet entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X of the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth) but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under that Part,
-- src:328 | or that the person has a substantially similar status under a law applicable in a place where the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth) does not apply.
@ref s 13D(2) (src:323-328)
GIVEN x IS A `Insolvency facts about a person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is a bankrupt or a person whose affairs are under insolvency laws` x MEANS
        `the person is a bankrupt` x
    OR  x's `a debtor party to a debt agreement under the Bankruptcy Act 1966 (Commonwealth)`
    OR  x's `a debtor who has entered a personal insolvency agreement under Part X and obligations remain to be discharged`
    OR  x's `not yet in a Part X agreement but has authorised a controlling trustee to perform functions under Part X`

§§ `14. References to 2 or more provisions to be inclusive`

-- Section 14: a reference by number or letter, or by number and letter, to 2 or more portions of a written law is
-- construed as including the portion described by the reference first-mentioned and the portion described by the
-- reference last-mentioned.  The portions are the labels of the law in order.
-- src:331 | A reference in a written law by number or letter or by number and letter to 2 or more portions of a written law shall be construed as including the portion described by the reference firstmentioned and the portion described by the reference lastmentioned.
@ref s 14 (src:331)
GIVEN last IS A STRING
      portions IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the portions up to and including` last `in` portions MEANS
    CONSIDER portions
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF p EQUALS last
        THEN LIST p
        ELSE p FOLLOWED BY (`the portions up to and including` last `in` rest)

@ref s 14 (src:331)
GIVEN portions IS A LIST OF STRING
      first IS A STRING
      last IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the portions a reference covers` portions first last MEANS
    CONSIDER portions
    WHEN EMPTY THEN EMPTY
    WHEN p FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        IF p EQUALS first
        THEN `the portions up to and including` last `in` portions
        ELSE `the portions a reference covers` rest first last

§§ `15. Internal references in written laws, construction of`

DECLARE `Kind of internal reference` IS ONE OF
    `a Part, Chapter, section, schedule, appendix or form`
    `a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of a provision`
    `a clause, subclause, paragraph or other division in a schedule`

DECLARE `What an internal reference points at` IS ONE OF
    `the Act in which the reference is made`
    `the provision in which the reference is made`
    `the schedule, or the provision of the schedule, in which the reference is made`
    `the other Act, provision or schedule the context indicates`

-- Section 15(1) to (3): a reference to a Part, Chapter, section, schedule, appendix or form is construed as a
-- reference to one of the Act in which the reference is made; a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph
-- or other division is construed as one of the provision in which it is made; a reference in a schedule to a clause,
-- subclause, paragraph or other division is construed as one of the schedule or of the provision of the schedule
-- in which it is made; in each case unless something in the context indicates a reference to some other Act,
-- provision or schedule.  Section 15(4): the three apply, subject to the necessary modifications, to subsidiary
-- legislation, which is read in place of the Act.
-- src:333 | (1) Where in an Act reference is made to a Part, Chapter, section, schedule, appendix, or form without anything in the context to indicate that a reference to a Part, Chapter, section, schedule, appendix, or form of or to some other Act is intended, the reference shall be construed as a reference to a Part, Chapter, section, schedule, appendix, or form of or to the Act in which the reference is made.
-- src:334 | (2) Where in a provision of an Act reference is made to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division without anything in the context to indicate that a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division of some other provision is intended, the reference shall be construed as a reference to a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph, or other division of the provision in which the reference is made.
-- src:335 | (3) Where in a schedule to an Act reference is made to a clause, subclause, paragraph or other division without anything in the context to indicate that a reference to a clause, subclause, paragraph, or other division of some other provision is intended, the reference shall be construed as a reference to a clause, subclause, paragraph, or other division of the schedule or provision of the schedule in which the reference is made.
-- src:336 | (4) The provisions of subsections (1), (2), and (3) shall apply, subject to the necessary modifications, to the construction of subsidiary legislation.
@ref s 15(1) (src:333)
@ref s 15(2) (src:334)
@ref s 15(3) (src:335)
@ref s 15(4) (src:336)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of internal reference`
      `something in the context indicates another one is intended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What an internal reference points at`
`an internal reference points at` kind `something in the context indicates another one is intended` MEANS
    IF `something in the context indicates another one is intended`
    THEN `the other Act, provision or schedule the context indicates`
    ELSE
        CONSIDER kind
        WHEN `a Part, Chapter, section, schedule, appendix or form` THEN `the Act in which the reference is made`
        WHEN `a subsection, paragraph, subparagraph or other division of a provision` THEN `the provision in which the reference is made`
        WHEN `a clause, subclause, paragraph or other division in a schedule` THEN `the schedule, or the provision of the schedule, in which the reference is made`

@ref s 15(4) (src:336)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of written law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 15(1) to (3) applies to the written law with the necessary modifications` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `subsidiary legislation` THEN TRUE

§§ `15A. Reference to paragraph`

DECLARE `Division of a written law` IS ONE OF
    `a paragraph`
    `a subparagraph`
    `an item`
    `a subitem`
    `any other similar provision`
    `a section`

-- Section 15A(1): in this section, paragraph includes a subparagraph, item, subitem and any other similar
-- provision.  A section is not so described (NOTHING).
-- src:338 | (1) In this section —
-- src:339 | paragraph includes a subparagraph, item, subitem and any other similar provision.
@ref s 15A(1) (src:338-339)
GIVEN x IS A `Division of a written law`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to a paragraph includes` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `a section` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- Section 15A(2): a reference in a written law to a paragraph includes a reference to a conjunction after it
-- connecting it to another paragraph.
-- src:340 | (2) A reference in a written law to a paragraph includes a reference to a conjunction after it connecting it to another paragraph.
@ref s 15A(2) (src:340)
GIVEN `the conjunction comes after the paragraph and connects it to another paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a reference to a paragraph includes the conjunction` `the conjunction comes after the paragraph and connects it to another paragraph` MEANS
    IF `the conjunction comes after the paragraph and connects it to another paragraph` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§§ `16. Reference to written law is to written law as amended`

DECLARE `What a reference in a written law refers to` IS ONE OF
    `a written law`
    `a provision of a written law`
    `an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act`
    `a provision of an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act`
    `a document that is not a written law`

-- Section 16: a reference in a written law to a written law, or to a provision of one, or to an Imperial Act or
-- a Commonwealth Act, or to a provision of one, is construed as including the law or provision as it may from time
-- to time be amended.  A document that is not a written law is not reached (NOTHING).
-- src:343 | (1) A reference in a written law to a written law shall be deemed to include a reference to such written law as it may from time to time be amended.
-- src:344 | (2) A reference in a written law to a provision of a written law shall be construed as a reference to such provision as it may from time to time be amended.
-- src:345 | (3) A reference in a written law to an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act, or to a provision of an Imperial Act or a Commonwealth Act, shall be construed so as to include a reference to such Act or provision as it may from time to time be amended.
@ref s 16(1) (src:343)
@ref s 16(2) (src:344)
@ref s 16(3) (src:345)
GIVEN x IS A `What a reference in a written law refers to`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference includes the law as it may from time to time be amended` x MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `a document that is not a written law` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `17. Disjunctive construction of "or"`

DECLARE `Word read disjunctively` IS ONE OF
    `the word or`
    `the word other`
    `the word otherwise`

-- Section 17: in relation to a written law passed or made after the commencement of this Act, but subject to s 3(3),
-- or, other and otherwise are construed disjunctively and not as implying similarity unless the word "similar" or
-- some other word of like meaning is added.  For a law not passed or made after the commencement (as s 3(3) reads
-- that) the section says nothing (NOTHING).  JUST TRUE means "read disjunctively, not as implying similarity".
-- src:347 | In relation to a written law passed or made after the commencement of this Act, but subject to section 3(3), or, other, and otherwise shall be construed disjunctively and not as implying similarity unless the word “similar” or some other word of like meaning is added.
@ref s 17 (src:347)
GIVEN w IS A `Word read disjunctively`
      `the day the written law was passed or made` IS A DATE
      `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the word similar, or some other word of like meaning, is added` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the word is read disjunctively and not as implying similarity` w `the day the written law was passed or made` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law` `the word similar, or some other word of like meaning, is added` MEANS
    IF `counts as passed or made after the commencement for ss 17, 25, 43(6), 50 and 64` `the day the written law was passed or made` `it continues or directly amends, but does not repeal entirely, the text of an existing written law`
    THEN JUST (NOT `the word similar, or some other word of like meaning, is added`)
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `18. Purpose or object of written law, use of in interpretation`

DECLARE `Construction preferred under section 18` IS ONE OF
    `the first construction`
    `the second construction`
    `neither is preferred by this section`

-- Section 18: in the interpretation of a provision, a construction that would promote the purpose or object
-- underlying the written law (whether expressly stated or not) is preferred to a construction that would not.
-- Whether a construction promotes the purpose or object is a judgment: a plain input for each construction.
-- Where both promote it, or neither does, the section does not choose.
-- src:349 | In the interpretation of a provision of a written law, a construction that would promote the purpose or object underlying the written law (whether that purpose or object is expressly stated in the written law or not) shall be preferred to a construction that would not promote that purpose or object.
@ref s 18 (src:349)
GIVEN `the first construction promotes the purpose or object` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second construction promotes the purpose or object` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Construction preferred under section 18`
`the construction preferred` `the first construction promotes the purpose or object` `the second construction promotes the purpose or object` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the first construction promotes the purpose or object` AND (NOT `the second construction promotes the purpose or object`) THEN `the first construction`
           IF `the second construction promotes the purpose or object` AND (NOT `the first construction promotes the purpose or object`) THEN `the second construction`
           OTHERWISE `neither is preferred by this section`

§§ `19. Extrinsic material, use of in interpretation`

DECLARE `Reason for looking at extrinsic material` IS ONE OF
    `to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context and the purpose or object`
    `because the provision is ambiguous or obscure`
    `because the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable`
    `for some other reason`

-- Section 19(1): subject to (3), if material not forming part of the written law is capable of assisting in the
-- ascertainment of the meaning of a provision, consideration may be given to it (a) to confirm that the meaning is
-- the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking into account its context and the purpose or object; or (b) to
-- determine the meaning when (i) the provision is ambiguous or obscure, or (ii) the ordinary meaning leads to a
-- result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable.  For any other reason the section does not allow it (FALSE:
-- (1) lists the occasions).  Whether the material is "capable of assisting" is a judgment: a plain input.
-- src:351 | (1) Subject to subsection (3), in the interpretation of a provision of a written law, if any material not forming part of the written law is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision, consideration may be given to that material —
-- src:352 | (a) to confirm that the meaning of the provision is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the written law and the purpose or object underlying the written law; or
-- src:353 | (b) to determine the meaning of the provision when —
-- src:354 | (i) the provision is ambiguous or obscure; or
-- src:355 | (ii) the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the written law and the purpose or object underlying the written law leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable.
@ref s 19(1) (src:351-355)
GIVEN `the material is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      why IS A `Reason for looking at extrinsic material`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`consideration may be given to the material` `the material is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning of the provision` why MEANS
        `the material is capable of assisting in ascertaining the meaning of the provision`
    AND CONSIDER why
        WHEN `to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context and the purpose or object` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `because the provision is ambiguous or obscure` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `because the ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `for some other reason` THEN FALSE

DECLARE `Kind of extrinsic material` IS ONE OF
    `a matter not forming part of the law, set out in an official version of the law under the Legislation Act 2021`
    `a report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body, laid before either House of Parliament`
    `a report of a committee of Parliament or of either House, made to Parliament or that House`
    `a treaty or other international agreement referred to in the written law`
    `an explanatory memorandum, or other relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of either House by a Minister`
    `the speech of a Minister moving the second reading of the Bill in a House`
    `a document declared by the written law to be a relevant document for the purposes of section 19`
    `relevant material in an official record of proceedings in either House`
    `material of some other kind`

-- Section 19(2): without limiting (1), the material that may be considered includes (a) to (h).  Three of the kinds
-- (reports laid, committee reports, explanatory memoranda) are limited to those made or laid before the time
-- when the provision was enacted.  Material of another kind is left to s 19(1) alone (NOTHING).
-- src:356 | (2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the material that may be considered in accordance with that subsection in the interpretation of a provision of a written law includes —
-- src:357 | (a) all matters not forming part of the written law that are set out in an official version of the law under the Legislation Act 2021; and
-- src:358 | (b) any relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body that was laid before either House of Parliament before the time when the provision was enacted; and
-- src:359 | (c) any relevant report of a committee of Parliament or of either House of Parliament that was made to Parliament or that House of Parliament before the time when the provision was enacted; and
-- src:360 | (d) any treaty or other international agreement that is referred to in the written law; and
-- src:361 | (e) any explanatory memorandum relating to the Bill containing the provision, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or furnished to the members of, either House of Parliament by a Minister before the time when the provision was enacted; and
-- src:362 | (f) the speech made to a House of Parliament by a Minister on the occasion of the moving of a motion that the Bill containing the provision be read a second time in that House; and
-- src:363 | (g) any document (whether or not a document to which a preceding paragraph applies) that is declared by the written law to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section; and
-- src:364 | (h) any relevant material in any official record of proceedings in either House of Parliament.
@ref s 19(2) (src:356-364)
GIVEN x IS A `Kind of extrinsic material`
      `it was laid, made or furnished before the provision was enacted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`material of this kind is among the material that may be considered` x `it was laid, made or furnished before the provision was enacted` MEANS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN `a matter not forming part of the law, set out in an official version of the law under the Legislation Act 2021` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission, committee of inquiry or other similar body, laid before either House of Parliament` THEN JUST `it was laid, made or furnished before the provision was enacted`
    WHEN `a report of a committee of Parliament or of either House, made to Parliament or that House` THEN JUST `it was laid, made or furnished before the provision was enacted`
    WHEN `a treaty or other international agreement referred to in the written law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `an explanatory memorandum, or other relevant document, laid before or furnished to the members of either House by a Minister` THEN JUST `it was laid, made or furnished before the provision was enacted`
    WHEN `the speech of a Minister moving the second reading of the Bill in a House` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a document declared by the written law to be a relevant document for the purposes of section 19` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `relevant material in an official record of proceedings in either House` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `material of some other kind` THEN NOTHING

-- Section 19(3): in deciding whether to consider material, or what weight to give it, regard is to be had, in
-- addition to any other relevant matters, to (a) the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary
-- meaning conveyed by the text, taking into account its context and the purpose or object; and (b) the need to
-- avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage.
-- src:365 | (3) In determining whether consideration should be given to any material in accordance with subsection (1), or in considering the weight to be given to any such material, regard shall be had, in addition to any other relevant matters, to —
-- src:366 | (a) the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the written law and the purpose or object underlying the written law; and
-- src:367 | (b) the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage.
@ref s 19(3) (src:365-367)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`the matters regard must be had to when deciding whether to consider material, and what weight to give it` MEANS
    LIST "the desirability of persons being able to rely on the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context and the purpose or object underlying the written law",
         "the need to avoid prolonging legal or other proceedings without compensating advantage"
